The DVD scrambling, payload-channel mapping, A5/92 texture strategy and measured
media presets are adapted from or informed by DiscImageStudio:
https://github.com/JiaFeiMiao-K-Cat/DiscImageStudio
Reference commit: c720fd45b76dc4d9257316474dd646a91589ffdb
Copyright DiscImageStudio authors and contributors, GPL-3.0-or-later.
See src/DvdImageSolver/Encoding/DvdDataFrameBuilder.cs,
src/DvdImageSolver/Encoding/DvdEccBlockEncoder.cs,
src/DvdImageSolver/Solver/FastDispersionImageWriter.cs,
src/DiscImageStudio.Core/DvdTrackGeometry.cs, and
src/DiscImageStudio.Core/Presets/built-in-disc-presets.json in that project.
Measured presets were contributed upstream by H4CNPE, Disappear9, DBPolp,
EternalEve, bczhc and other DiscImageStudio contributors. They are not universal
calibrations for every drive or every disc with the same marketing name.

Calibration address-band intervals and the continuous phase-difference method
are informed by the same reference commit's docs/CALIBRATION.md and
src/DiscImageStudio.Core/Calibration/CalibrationWideBandPattern.cs,
CalibrationCrossPrediction.cs, CalibrationCrossFitter.cs and CalibrationFitter.cs.
The Go fitter, browser photo measurement workflow and persistence code are
implemented for this application. The Maxell DVD+R preset is nominal, not an
upstream measured calibration.

